Source: tolome-dada
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Anhky <dev@tolome.net>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: tolome-dada
Architecture: all
Depends: sudo-rs (>= 0.2), sudo, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: bash-completion
Suggests: nala
Description: "dada" administration command of Tolome, based on sudo-rs
 "dada" ("His Majesty" in Fon) runs a command with administrator rights through
 sudo-rs, the Rust implementation of sudo:
 .
   dada nala install vim
 .
 It adds no policy: the rules stay in /etc/sudoers and /etc/sudoers.d. The
 classic "sudo" command stays installed for compatibility (its PAM files are
 shared with sudo-rs). Bash completion and a manual page in French are
 provided. Removing this package only removes "dada".
